A new rule, ledger/no-unknown-variant, in both presets at error, with a Lint.mdx row and a case file. It sits after no-dark-variant in classify's precedence.
A pure variantKnown(variant, grammar) lives in classes.js (prototype: scratch/harvest-oracle/variant-check.mjs, 35 lines):
- an arbitrary [..] variant passes;
- a trailing /name is stripped;
- a static name must match exactly;
- otherwise the longest functional root wins;
- compound roots (not, group, peer, in, has) recurse, and a compound that takes no /name hands it to what it wraps;
- functional values come from the value list, or anyName, integer or arbitrary.
ARIA: an aria-<name> variant requires <name> in lint.json.ariaNames (51 names). The bracket form checks too.
Suggestions, never --fix, go through fixes.js with closure:
- one edit only;
- except a compound root up to two edits away around an exact inner (grp-hover → group-hover);
- ARIA names within 1 edit, or 2 for names of 6+ characters, unique only;
- never respell a breakpoint or container; list them with their values instead.
One report per class. If the base is also unknown, one replacement fixes both, only when both fixes are unique. The replacement keeps the other variants and `!`.

